    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1067">

                <pb facs="1113" n="1101" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/5–2545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-25T16:00:00+02:00">May 25, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2957. My tel. 2956, May 25.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d1067-f1"/> In view of
                    Bidault’s statement regarding Syria and Lebanon I suggest that the proposal set
                    out in Depts 2271, May 23, be held in abeyance for a few days.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept as 2957, rptd London as 340.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
